WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:20.320
Thank you all people from Dawlish for helping
us and thank you for all people of England

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.160
that hosted Ukrainians

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:30.130
I just want to say thank you to my host family
in Dawlish for all the tremendous help and

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:36.989
support they provided me during this year. That empowered me to be better and braver.

00:00:36.989 --> 00:00:41.079
Thank you one more time to everyone who supports
Ukraine.

00:00:41.079 --> 00:00:48.510
I'd like to say big thank you to my host family
and I really appreciate your support during

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.790
such difficult times for me and for all Ukrainians.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:58.190
When I was in despair you were trying to distract
me and show the positive side of my life and

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:06.150
I'll always remember our fascinating trips
to Longleat, Dartmoor and the ones like cooking,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.000
[INDISTINGUISHABLE] , and watching movies together.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:13.350
As I said it was fun and such a great cultural
exchange in my life.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:18.430
I guess during these times you became as the
second family for me because you're always

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:25.500
worried about me, literally I've never met
such kind and generous people in my life.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:29.250
I want to say thank you so much.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:35.700
I'm so grateful to my host family who gave
us not only home and the family as well.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.040
Rosie is like a sister and her family became
native to us.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.689
Thanks everyone for supporting Ukraine.

00:01:42.689 --> 00:01:51.009
Dear host I would like to say thank you to
each of you for this opportunity you have

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:54.920
given to Ukrainian families.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:02:03.490
For the fact that the majority of those currently
in Britain have support and feel safe.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:11.170
For the fact that we have the opportunity
to continue to work and enjoy peaceful life.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:18.870
[Music] We're very grateful to you for your
kindness and support.

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:24.770
You have opened not only doors of your house
but also your heart.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:38.330
[text appears with photo of Ukrainian girl]
With great gratitude for giving us a peaceful

00:02:38.330 --> 00:02:55.430
sky above our heads, the opportunity to get
to know your country and much more!

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.920
Thank you!

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:06.409
Dear Erica and John I want to thank you so
much for all that you have done and do for

00:03:06.409 --> 00:03:08.000
our family.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:13.080
Thank you for sharing and sheltering you from
the war.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:21.080
Thank you for the house, uh thank you for
the security, thank you for the silence which

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.510
is not possible in Ukraine.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:30.490
My children are happy and smiling which is
the most important thing for me.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:38.610
Dear John and Erica thank you for saving me
from the war and giving me a house where I

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:45.599
live in comfort and safety and do not hear
the sound of bombs and sirens.

00:03:45.599 --> 00:03:47.832
Thank you for everything

00:03:47.832 --> 00:03:55.099
Dear Erica and John thank you for the help and save me from the war, and help me.

00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:55.099
 

00:03:55.099 --> 00:03:56.450
I'm very glad that we met.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:56.450
 

00:03:56.054 --> 00:03:57.450
text which reads: on 9th June we celebrated
our 'second birthday', our one year anniversary

00:03:57.450 --> 00:03:58.450
in England.

00:03:58.450 --> 00:03:59.450
We lost Ukrainian family, but found an English
one.

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:00.450
Every single day we thank God for our hosting
family as they are truly amazing, kind-hearted,

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:01.450
very generous, supportive, loving, caring,
genuine and wonderful people, who saved our

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:02.450
lives, helped us to stand on our own feet
and gave us hope for a better future.

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:03.450
We live like one big family.

00:04:03.450 --> 00:04:11.390
We introduced our Ukrainian cuisine to our
English family and they liked our dishes a

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:12.390
lot.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:22.699
We happily share Ukrainian and English recipes,
trying something new and healthy at the same

00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:23.699
time.

00:04:23.699 --> 00:04:29.270
Thank you for the help and care, your support
is very important to us.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:32.940
Thank you for all this help that you give
us.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:43.290
We are very proud for this fact that you drop
to welcome complete strangers from another

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:46.340
country into your home.

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:56.680
You didn't just open the doors to your home;
you had opened the possibility for my family

00:04:56.680 --> 00:05:09.410
to see the sky where there aren't... doesn't
feel without explosions in area.

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:15.220
xxx Thank you, many thank you
Thank you

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:21.050
Thank you
Thank you we love you

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:27.100
We would like to sincerely thanks to our host
family who supported us throughout all the

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:28.910
time we stay here.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:38.270
We would like to say thank you for shared
with us not just a house, food and time, but

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:43.610
love patience, exception and compassion.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:52.840
We also would like to say thank you to all
volunteers, workers of different institutions,

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:59.960
teachers, everybody who is kind to us and
who help us every day.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:04.910
Thank you to all of the amazing Dawlish community
- you are incredible people!

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:10.942
You give us strength, determination, courage
and hope for a better future.

00:06:10.942 --> 00:06:11.942
Thank you.

00:06:11.942 --> 00:06:12.942
Thank you from all of us.

00:06:12.942 --> 00:06:13.942
[text]"I'm very grateful to our host family,
they are wonderful people with big hearts."

00:06:13.942 --> 00:06:14.942
"Our hosts are very sensitive people, their
support inspires me, even now, when I have

00:06:14.942 --> 00:06:15.942
not been home for a year.

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:16.942
I try to move on and build a future with their
help."

00:06:16.942 --> 00:06:17.942
"We feel safe here and not forgotten"
"I'm glad I made the decision to take the

00:06:17.942 --> 00:06:18.942
baby to a safe place.

00:06:18.942 --> 00:06:19.942
Her smile and happy eyes are more important
than anything in the world.")

00:06:19.942 --> 00:06:20.942
[text] (message to host families) You have opened
your hearts and homes, having a huge impact

00:06:20.942 --> 00:06:21.942
on many people.

00:06:21.942 --> 00:06:22.942
We celebrate you, your families and all who
have offered support to our guests from Ukraine.

00:06:22.942 --> 00:06:23.442
Ends

